A||N||11||Bigfieroman||Stupid ticket...damnit!||||1||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||05-31-2001||09:25 PM||||I just got one for 29.6 in a school zone:  I was following this woman down a hill who was going about 5-10 MPH and hitting her brakes randomly.  I was watching her so I didn't hit her.  In between brake slams, I was looking ahead to see that there was a cemet truck blocking the road, along with some cars waiting to pull into a driveway.  I never saw the school zone sign as I drove past.  So this woman apparently finds the correct address, and pulls in with no turn signal.  I waited for about 2 minutes as the waiting car pulled in, and then I pulled away, past the school.  At the VERY END of the school zone, there was a cop waiting at the vascar lines, who clocked me at 29.6 in a 15 zone.  It happened today, on the 31th of the month, the last day to make his quota.  He wouldn't hear what I had to say, went back to his car, and came back with a ticket in less than 5 minutes.  Apparently, he already had the ticket written.  Also, he spelled my name wrong, which offers another route in my argument.  Can you guys help me out? any idead? thanks!<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||05-31-2001||09:52 PM||||I hope that S.O.B. gets testicular cancer from his radar gun.<P>I often drive through two school zones on my way to work.  One is a high school on a new street with no other buildings for 1/2 mile in any direction...totally deserted and all the kids ride the bus or drive to school.  Yet half the time there's a cop there making sure no one goes 21 mph!<P>The other school zone is a grade school on a 4-lane road in the middle of a crowded neighborhood.  I see people drive 35-40 mph past the school - even when small children are walking around.  But I've never seen a cop around to slow them down.  Go figure...<P>I respect police officers - except when they serve as tax collectors.<P>Sorry, bigfieroman, but you'll never get out of that ticket (unless your real name is O.J.).<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000002||84Bill||05-31-2001||11:25 PM||||Sorry you got a ticket bub. school zones I'll have to say they are a pain in the ass but since I have a school age kid myself I think its best to slow it down and watch everything. damn kids will appear from vapor and try their hardest to make you run em over. Some day you will know exactly what I'm saying   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> On the limited access highway go as fast as ya want but back streets and school zones be extra carefull.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Flat squrrals fly great! Flat kids well lets just leave it at that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||Standard||05-31-2001||11:30 PM||||Hate to play devil's advocate here...  but you were going twice the speed limit in a school zone...||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||05-31-2001||11:58 PM||||Welcome to my world. Cops love me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">    <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||06-01-2001||12:15 AM||||I had some kid on a bike ride right in front of me the other day. Speed limit is 45mph, with moderate traffic. I was cruising at 45 approaching a side street. Kid on the bike was on the side street and never even looked either direction. I had no stop sign, warning sign or anything, he had the stop sign. Luckily the intersection was very open and I could tell he wasn't paying attention so I was able to slow down and let dumba$$ pop right out in front of me. Kid was at least 14 years old, why wasn't he in school at 1pm, or look before crossing the street. If there had been bushes blocking my view...I don't know how a bike fares when a Fiero hits it at 45mph, but I doubt very well.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steve Normington||06-01-2001||12:16 AM||||It is my understanding that you can accelerate above 15 mph once you are past the crosswalk. Where were you when he clocked you?<P>PS. This is in Az, your laws may vary.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||06-01-2001||09:33 AM||||In GA, the beginning and end of school zones are clearly marked. The cops take school zones really seriously, too. You MIGHT get away with 5-10 over, but that is pushing it. Kids are unpredictable. Ya' never know...<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000008||drednot||06-01-2001||10:44 AM||||F U C K I N G COPS!!!  Why can't they just DIE!  Seriously though, I hate Tickets!||||reg||4
Z||000009||DRH||06-01-2001||11:50 AM||||Probably your best shot is to go to court. If the cop doesn't show up for court, most places will throw it out. This happens more often than you might think.<P>If he does show up, you are 99.9% sure to be found guilty most places. Your best hope then is to plead your case to the judge about extenuating circumstances and try for a reduced fine. I wouldn't mention the meeting his quota type stuff to the judge, that'll just pi$$ him off. Take responsibility for what you did, explain the reasons (not excuses), show remorse, and ask for leniency...<P>Some places the DA's office will call you when you ask for a court date and try for a plea bargain. If they offer you a decent deal, I'd go for it.<P>Good luck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||06-01-2001||12:25 PM||||I was going to the local Best Buy the other day with one of my friends (I was driving).  Well, the road that goes around the outside of the mall is a 35mph zone.  I was doing almost 40mph.  Well, I happen to notice these two kids crossing the left lane (there is a median between the two sides).  I didn't think much of it because there were few cars on that side, but the morons didn't even wait on the median for me <I>or</I> the rest of the cars I was with to pass before walking out.  I do believe that that is jay walking!  (And just stupid.)  Hm.  A group of 5 or 6 cars doing at least 40mph and they walk out like 30 feet in front of me.  I was already starting to slow down for them (guessing that they were going to be stupid) but the people next to me had no idea and had to SLAM on their breaks... screeching tires and everything.  And what do these two morons do?  They flick off me and the driver of the car that had to slam on the breaks.  Where are the cops when you need 'em?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-01-2001||03:06 PM||||holy cow - where is all this coming from?!<P>last year a 3rd grader in my town was hit by a car right in front of his school on a snowy morning. Driver couldnt stop - going too fast for the weather conditions<P>3 years ago a high school student was hit right in front of the high school. By the time the ambulance got there he was dead.<P>I use to drop my son off at his middle school, cause it was right on my way to work and saved him a half hour on the bus in the morning. Whenever I pulled out in my big-ol rusty full sized dodge van, if someone was coming through the 25mph school zone (with the yellow lights flashing) at 35 or 40 or more, i would time it just right and pull right out in front of them, slowly, making them come to a dead stop, then I would stare them down - daring them to step out of the car and say something.<P>  I know it seems stupid to be putting past a school at 15 or 25mph, esp when classes have already started and there are no students to be seen anywhere<P>   but that is exactly when some kid who is late for school will try to dart across the street - and he expects you to be going 15mph, not 30.<P>  Sorry - no sympathy from me - you were pissed at the lady who was driving slow and 10:1 you nailed it once you got past her, no?<P>Once you have attended the funeral for a 16 year old kid whos only mistake was stepping back off a curb in a split second error of judgment, your attitude will be adjusted.<P>  BTW, I am pretty sure in all 50 states and Canada, if someone is crossing the street, even if they are on the median, in a parking lot, or even if they are J walking, they have the right of way and you are REQUIRED to stop and let them pass. If they are in the wrong it doesnt matter - pedestrians always have the right of way.<P>  In canada esp, if a pedistrain steps onto a cross walk all the way on the other side of the street, even if its 4 lanes on both sides, its the same as a red light and you have to stop till he is all the way across the street. canadian cops will write you up in a second if you dont.<P>  Geeze people, whats the big deal, drop it down into 2nd or 3rd, putter through at clutch speed, put a little mental chalk mark in your column under 'did something good today' - slowed down for a school zone or stopped and let a pedestrian cross - invested 5 seconds towards a better society.<P>  If you drive 1/10th of a mph faster for the rest of the trip you will make up the lost 5 seconds.<P>  make it a ritual - sing the "Im driving 15 miles per hour in a school zone, casue Im one awesome dude" song. by the time you get to the 3rd verse you will be on the other side.<P>  arnt there any boy scouts left in the world? or are they all on the Dodge caravan forum?<P>To be fair (I know a bunch of you already think I am narrow minded, preachy and a PITA) I am not a saint either - I've gotten my share of speeding tickets<P>  I was driving across PA on highway 6 on Memorial day weekend several years back, family in the dodge van, heading home from a weekend of backpacking, had the cruise control set at 55 the whole way, line of cars behind me half the time, and I come around  a bend and see a mile long streach of straight road, and a station wagon with a trailer had just pulled out, going about 40.<P>  I figured Id be a nice guy and pass him as quick as possible and give some of the cars behind me time to pass too, so I floored it, let the mighty 5.2L V8 open up, passed the guy cleanly, pull back into the right lane (2 lane road) and there is a PA state trooper right in my rear view mirror.<P>   Clocked me going 70 in the 55. I never even looked at the speedo while passing - was only thinking 'pass and get back on the right side of the road'.<P>  You're not allowed to speed to pass someone (hows that for stupid?)<P>   thing that PO'd me the most was I drove over 400 miles that weekend with the cruise control set to the speed limit, and for that 30 seconds while i was passing someone - I got nailed.<P>  Okay, I'll give you a little sympathy - it is pretty demeaning having the smokey with the gun and the flashing red lights hand you a ticket with the stearn face, esp with your family in the vehicle with you. It would be less traumatic if they put out a little machine that photographed your car as you sped by, recorded your speed and mailed the ticket to you.<P>  But thats the way it is - its not a hard game to play - its not like the signs are hidden or something (usually).<P>  When you get outside town, out in the clear, and you wanna open it up a little, you know your car, know your abilities, there is nothing magical about 65mph, or 70 or 80 - its not like is a mortal sin or anything.<P>  but in town, in a residentail area, past a school, what the heck, putt along, stick you elbow out the window, set the cruise control, give everyone plenty of time to drool on their shoes while they stare at your car, lean back in your seat, and sing quietly: <P>"Im one awesome dude<BR>with one awesome car<BR>I could be going 102<BR>if I wanted,<P>but Im too cool for that..."<P>  [stepping down from soap box now before I fall and hurt myself]||||reg||1
